# Hospital Inpatient Flow & Clinical Risk Command Center

An end-to-end healthcare analytics dashboard built in **Power BI** powered by a **PostgreSQL** database. It monitors inpatient capacity, 30-day readmission risk, biomarker severity, and Social Determinants of Health (SDoH) across 10,000 patient encounters[cite: 2].

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack
- **Database:** PostgreSQL (`Healthcare_analytics`)
- **Data Pipeline:** Python (Pandas, SQLAlchemy)
- **BI Platform:** Power BI Desktop
- **Calculations:** DAX (`_Measures` table)[cite: 1]

---

## 📌 Key Metrics & Visuals
- **Executive KPIs:** Total Inpatient Volume (10K), High-Risk Readmission Rate (33.3%), Avg Length of Stay (15.1 days), Bed Days (151K), and Acuity Index (2.21).
- **Clinical Acuity Scatter:** Serum creatinine vs. glucose levels by comorbidity[cite: 2].
- **Comorbidity Risk Breakdown:** 100% stacked bar chart of readmission tiers across conditions.
- **Payer Mix Donut:** High-risk volume distribution across insurance classes.
- **Biomarker Matrix:** Cross-analysis of glycemic status and admission types.
- **SDoH & Adherence:** Post-discharge compliance segmented by social support.
- **Operational Bed Flow:** Inpatient volume vs. readmission rate across length-of-stay tiers.

---

## 🚀 Getting Started
1. Load patient encounter data into PostgreSQL (`localhost:5432`).
2. Open the `.pbix` file in Power BI Desktop.
3. Update data source credentials under **Transform Data > Data Source Settings** to point to your local PostgreSQL instance.
4. Hit **Refresh** to load the visual reports.
